# chromium: Chromium's Linux code built for Jam OS (docs/CR-PLAN.md
# sections 14 and 15, track CB1): the source tarball Alpine's chromium uses
# (the chromium-linux-tarballs project's, no .git; Alpine's stable, which
# the version follows), Alpine's and copium's musl patches as Alpine applies
# them (patches/00*, 01*: each one's reason in its header), and Jam OS's own
# (09*: the GN toolchain //build/toolchain/jamos:x64). Built with Chromium's
# own GN, its pinned clang and Rust (tools/cr/toolchain.sh), for
# x86_64-unknown-linux-musl against the port's sysroot, linked static and
# position-dependent by tools/jamos-clang. The build is huge: its source and
# output stay between builds (`tree kept`, tools/portslib/kept.py), on the
# PC under ~/cr (tools/cr/build.sh, which starts it there at low priority
# with a claim in the machine's budget). It builds only on the build host
# (Linux x86_64: Chromium's tools are Linux binaries).
#
# CB1 builds base_unittests and headless_shell (files/args.gn); CB2 runs
# the first, CB3 the second; CB4 adds content_shell, on the desktop
# (Ozone's Wayland). The programs' lists are wants/<name>: each program
# needs its `program` line below, as the link takes a program's list from
# there (one linked without it asks only for `posix`, so it starts with
# no /data). The
# licence line is Chromium's own; the third parties' licences (its
# about:credits) come with the `chrome` target (CB6).
name        chromium
version     155.0.8059.39
revision    1
summary     the Chromium web browser's code: base_unittests, headless_shell and content_shell
homepage    https://www.chromium.org/
category    www
licence     BSD-3-Clause
licence-file LICENSE
source      https://github.com/chromium-linux-tarballs/chromium-tarballs/releases/download/$version/chromium-$version-linux.tar.xz 2021203420 b84bbab0eef2dd4abd73544a95f15dd2c3c815980c4fa47496f3d0ce4f8a2aa7
place       package
style       custom
toolchain   clang rust
tree        kept
# No `image-base` yet (docs/CR-PLAN.md, MH): linked at 1 TiB, headless_shell
# can't be, as BoringSSL calls weak functions nothing defines
# (OPENSSL_memory_alloc, _free), which a static non-PIE link puts at 0,
# beyond a call's 2 GiB from 1 TiB. Linux links Chromium as a PIE (at 0, so
# 0 is near); the way here is a static PIE the loader places high.
needs       llvm-runtimes
# Wayland's (Chromium's own copy of libwayland links libffi), and what
# Chromium takes from the system on Linux: the keyboard's (pkg-config) and
# expat (fontconfig's and Skia's XML). zlib: FFmpeg's build links the
# system's libz on every POSIX system but Android and Fuchsia (Chromium's
# own zlib, which everything else uses, has its symbols renamed).
needs       libffi
needs       xkbcommon
needs       expat
needs       zlib
host        python3 ninja
program     lib/chromium/base_unittests
program     lib/chromium/test_child_process
program     lib/chromium/headless_shell
files       lib/chromium/headless_lib_data.pak lib/chromium/headless_lib_strings.pak
files       lib/chromium/headless_command_resources.pak
program     lib/chromium/content_shell
files       lib/chromium/content_shell.pak
